    "## Question 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Question 1 asks us to implement functions to encrypt and decrypt the Ceasar and Viginere ciphers for alphabetic characters only. \n",
    "\n",
    "The Caesar cipher uses a number from 0-25 as the key and shifts the plaintext this many places in the alphabet. \n",
    "\n",
    "The Vigenere cipher takes a string of letters repeated as long as the plaintext as the key, converts them to their number place in the alphabet (e.g. A=0, B=1,...) and performs an individual caesar cipher for each letter in the plaintext, based on the corresponding number from the key. \n"
   ]
  },
