   "source": [
    "Next, to encrypt the Vigenere cipher, the function takes a plaintext and a key, iterates through each letter in the key and the plaintext, works out the corresponding caesar key and performs the ceasar cipher on the plaintext letter.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the key might not be as long as the plaintext, the modulo function is used so the index of the key does not go out of range. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "14232300-731f-4145-a8aa-f6b5a17c1a50",
   "metadata": {},
