   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Discussion\n",
    "\n",
    "The extension allows us to systematically break a Vigenère cipher without knowing the key. However, as demonstrated by running the trials, we need a considerable amount of text to correctly identify enough repeated 3-grams, and even more to perform successful frequency analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following results were obtained from a test run I performed myself. Note results will vary between runs as I did not seed the randomness.\n",
    "\n",
    "For texts of length 100 and a key length of 4, Kasiski analysis failed to identify the key length in 18 trials. The process was successful once, and frequency analysis failed in another.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a text length of 5,000 and a key length of 6, out of 10 trials we achieved 9 successes and 1 failure due to frequency analysis. Increasing the text length by another 5,000 characters to 10,000 meant in this case still resulted in one frequency analysis failiure, but 9 successes.\n",
    "\n",
    "In an attempt to discard anomalies that could negatively affect the key length calculation, we ignore keys of length 1 and 2, meaning that we would not be able to detect keys of these lengths. Also key lengths longer than the length of the ciphertext/20 are discarded as anomalies too, not enough characters would be returned for frequency analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "Testing also resulted in a change to the frequency analysis method, as, in our testing, simply looking at the most frequent character yields more reliable results.\n",
    "\n",
    "The key search, i.e. finding repeated 3-grams, also takes some time when looping through large amounts of text. However, for text lengths of up to 10,000 characters, it completes in a reasonable amount of time.\n",
    "\n",
    "The trial text also comes from the master text, the same text used to produce a table of English language frequencies, which could flatter the results a bit but is still suitable for our purposes.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
